  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Labour Market Information and Labour Market Information Systems in the Caribbean for more and better jobs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging the foundation of a long-term partnership between the ILO and the Caribbean Community Secretariat (CARICOM), the ILO aims to strengthen the capacity of CARICOM and its member states in operationalizing integrated regional and national Labour Market Information Systems (LMIS). It provides technical assistance to the Organisation of Eastern Caribbean States (OECS) in designing, piloting, analyzing, and disseminating harmonized labour force surveys, and promote evidence-based formulation and implementation of national employment policies. The ILO&#x2019;s support focuses on data harmonization, launching the LMIS, and mentoring, as well as developing new questionnaires for labour force surveys in Grenada, Saint Lucia, and Dominica.

 

Beneficiaries of this initiative include CARICOM and OECS member states, which will gain from improved labour market statistics and enhanced national LMIS. The work will be done in collaboration with CARICOM, OECS, and national statistical offices, with the ILO providing technical guidance and support. This strategy aims to produce reliable labour market information, improve the design and implementation of economic and employment policies, and strengthen partnerships between CARICOM, OECS, and national labour market information units.</narrative>
  </description>
